<title>GERMANY: Opel says sees strong orders for new Vectra.</title>
<headline>Opel says sees strong orders for new Vectra.</headline>
<dateline>RUESSELSHEIM, Germany 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Adam Opel AG, a unit of U.S.-based General Motors Corp, said on Thursday that it has seen strong demand for its new Opel Vectra Caravan estate wagon with more than 25,000 orders so far.</p>
<p>Opel said the car, which will officially launched on November 16, will be available in Germany, Italy, the U.K., Austria and Switzerland.</p>
<p>Opel expects the new Vectra model to account for 40 percent of the overall Vectra product line output.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
